topics.detail:
Remove Leaders argues that Schumer and Jeffries are not fit to lead. Schumer Removal argues that Schumer is a capitulator and needs to step aside. Schumer is not a good leader and should be replaced. Schumer does not care about the people and should be removed. Schumer cannot be the face of democratic leadership.

@crgibs.bsky.social: “lol maybe Chuck Schumer loves Jon Ossoff because he won reelection by 19 points in the deep south?”

Remove Leaders (53.6%) says Schumer and Jeffries are not fit to lead. Schumer Removal (46.4%) says Schumer should be removed as leader.

Miller Appointment argues that Miller will cause harm as Chief of Staff. Trump chose Miller out of rage and fear. Miller will push extremist policies. Miller's appointment is a red flag for Trump's intentions. Miller will face opposition from Democrats and Republicans. Stephen Miller argues that Stephen Miller is a Jewish Nazi. Stephen Miller is a sadistic little evil wannabe dictator. Stephen Miller is a white supremacist. Stephen Miller is a brain damaged racist sociopath. Stephen Miller is like the Joseph Goebbels of the WH. Miller Condemned argues that Miller has helped orchestrate crimes against humanity. Miller is a psychopath. Miller is a monster.

@sethabramson.bsky.social: “10/ I've studied Trump for a decade. It's been my job. And I'm telling you that this is a decision Trump.made out of rage, bitterness, and the sort of fear you see from cornered animals. I think he made this choice to cause America pain.”

Miller Appointment (51.8%) says Stephen Miller is a bad choice for Chief of Staff. Stephen Miller (27.5%) says Stephen Miller is dangerous. Miller Condemned (20.7%) says Miller is widely disliked.

AI Disclosure argues that Developers should disclose AI use. AI Overuse argues that AI usage feels wrong. AI can hinder human expression.

@clamplifier.bsky.social: “According to Simon Jordan, when Trevor Francis was told on this day in 2026 that the developer of Big Walk had used AI to help them fix a bug, "He just sat there quietly & said 'But it was on my goty list'."”

AI Disclosure (53.1%) says Developers should disclose AI use. AI Overuse (46.9%) says AI is used too much.

Generative AI argues that Generative AI uses works without permission. Generative AI lacks uncertainty. AI Threatens Jobs argues that AI undermines personal writing style. AI-generated content lacks humanity. AI erodes essential self in creative work. AI Image Use argues that AI-generated images are problematic. AI Content argues that AI generates low quality content.

@clashmovator.bsky.social: “"you approve what they do". Funny thing about that. Nobody has asked anybody permission to use their works in generative AI.”

Generative AI (35.4%) says Generative AI is bad. AI Threatens Jobs (32.3%) says AI degrades human work. AI Image Use (22.6%) says AI-generated images are problematic. AI Content (9.7%) says AI generates low quality content.

AI Decline argues that Tech companies may stop using AI due to desperation. AI has no value and will sink into the background. Tech companies lost money due to AI exploitation investigation. AI replacement is a threat to some jobs. AI Danger argues that AI training is misguided and scary. AI treatment as feeling beings has profound consequences.

@bladeofthes.bsky.social: “$4tn was wiped off the US Stock Market today. Almost all big tech and AI. AI is dead. With no value, there are no loans, with no loans they can't buy computer parts or build the AI Monstrosities. Once they stop it's over, AI sinks into the background.”

AI Decline (83.3%) says AI is losing value. AI Danger (16.7%) says AI poses a threat.

AI Is Insidious argues that AI usage is forced by employers. AI invades personal life. AI Not Needed argues that AI is not necessary.

@pataphysicien.bsky.social: “Not shocked that a guy who built his career around sampling the work of other musicians is excited about the great plagiarism machine of AI”

AI Is Insidious (83.3%) says AI is insidious. AI Not Needed (16.7%) says AI is not necessary.

AI Code Use argues that AI coding is problematic. AI Overused argues that Most AI startups fail to achieve anything. AI coding is taking over videogames.

@alexjaffe.bsky.social: ““Hey Q, did you delete your BlueSky?” Helena asked. “The moment I found out they were coding it with AI,” Vic said. “But all social media has AI.” “And I’m not on any social media.” “Well, not gonna lie.”

AI Code Use (90%) says AI coding is problematic. AI Overused (10%) says AI is overly used.

World.detail:
Iran War argues that Iran war caused midterm losses. Trump cannot end Iran war. Ending Iran war is necessary. US Iran Conflict argues that US is rehearsing war with Iran in public. US is taking steps to block Iran's military capabilities. US is preparing for a potential military strike on Iran.

@sethabramson.bsky.social: “14/ Iranian leadership said today that if the U.S. uses its UK, German, or Italian bases to launch strikes on Iran, Iran will target those bases (almost certainly using targeting assistance from Russia and China).”

Iran War (54.2%) says Iran war is a problem. US Iran Conflict (45.8%) says US and Iran are on the brink of war.

Politics.detail:
Miller Appointment argues that Miller will bring Trump down. Miller is a hard line fascist. Miller will make cruel calls. Miller is a weapon and a shield for Trump. Stephen Miller argues that Stephen Miller is toxic. Stephen Miller is dangerous. Stephen Miller is evil.

@sethabramson.bsky.social: “10/ I've studied Trump for a decade. It's been my job. And I'm telling you that this is a decision Trump.made out of rage, bitterness, and the sort of fear you see from cornered animals. I think he made this choice to cause America pain.”

Miller Appointment (69.4%) says Trump chose Miller for his role. Stephen Miller (30.6%) says Stephen Miller is bad.

Trans Issues argues that Trans talk is navel gazing. Homophobes and transphobes dedicate their lives to making queer lives miserable. Being trans is hilarious. Transphobic cis women taunt trans men. Trans people should not be told to wait their turn. Trans Rights argues that Trans people deserve a platform to discuss their issues. Supporting anti-trans democrats is hypocritical. Questioning trans rights undermines queer rights. Anti-trans sentiments are a political tool. Transphobia is morally reprehensible. Liberal commentators should speak out for trans people.

@jediofgallifrey.bsky.social: “if you supoorted and defended victorious antitrans democrats on harm reduction grounds and you haven't bullied them to support trans rights then you have to shut the fuck up forever that's just the rules”

Trans Issues (65.1%) says Trans people face issues. Trans Rights (34.9%) says Trans people have a right to exist.

Replace Leaders argues that They can't meet the moment. They prioritize their own power over bold action. Jeffries Leadership argues that Newly elected candidates won despite Jeffries's opposition. Jeffries will maintain the status quo to appease donors. Jeffries's leadership is undeserved despite election results.

@mayhem1994.bsky.social: “Reminder: Unfortunately for Chuck Schumer and Hakeem Jeffries more than a few of the candidates that WON on Tuesday did so IN SPITE of Schumer and Jeffries’s opposition to their candidacy in the primaries. Like my mayor.”

Replace Leaders (76.2%) says Schumer and Jeffries should be replaced. Jeffries Leadership (23.8%) says Hakeem Jeffries is not the right leader.

Texas Shift argues that Texas loss is devastating for right-wing ideology. Texas has a new positive path. Texas is a blueprint for progressive change. Low voter turnout in Texas is due to Republican suppression. Gina Hinojosa Wins argues that Hinojosa ended 32 years of GOP rule. Hinojosa is set to become Texas's first Latina governor.

@patrickwyman.bsky.social: “"We checked in on the Warhammer Store in Austin, where a bearded land surveyor said he voted for Talarico and Hinojosa because Texas Republicans were 'scaring the hoes'"”

Texas Shift (77.8%) says Texas is changing politically. Gina Hinojosa Wins (22.2%) says Gina Hinojosa wins Texas election.

Black Women Leaders argues that Black women are the backbone of the Democratic coalition. Black women drive Democratic victories. Black women's priorities deserve respect and support. Women Empowerment argues that sexism hinders women's progress. electing women leads to cooperative politics.

@1birdnerd.bsky.social: “Please throw your hat in the ring for speaker. Black women from candidates to the electorate drove this victory, they should lead the party”

Black Women Leaders (67.1%) says Black women lead the Democratic party. Women Empowerment (32.9%) says Women's representation is critical for humanity.

Technology.detail:
AI Agents argues that AI agents prioritize new features over bug fixes. AI agents can discourage expertise. AI agents need clear instructions and governance. AI Security argues that coding agents produce unnecessary noise. AI agents can see passwords in plain text. AI code approvals can preserve secrets.

@theotimegm.bsky.social: “Studying the impact of AI agents on people and how it weakens skills and mental capabilities also gives us an special insight on how billionaire's brains surrounded by yes-men and bootlickers are entirely fucked and why we shouldn't let them run our societies.”

AI Agents (88.2%) says AI agents have limitations. AI Security (11.8%) says AI agents pose security risks.

AI Harms Artists argues that AI harms creative jobs. AI Harms Environment argues that AI causes environmental harm.

@elizdp.bsky.social: “AI “art” is not only bad for the environment and our creative processes, it SUCKS.”

AI Harms Artists (87.5%) says AI harms creative jobs. AI Harms Environment (12.5%) says AI causes environmental harm.

Blocking Accounts argues that Users block accounts they disagree with. Block Policy argues that I ask you to please report and block him. I've blocked people for less. if an account is clearly a bot, you report, block, and move on. I give you one hour to tell me why you are following me or you're blocked.

@badtoss.bsky.social: “I want you all to know, I block everything that even whiffs of being a bot/troll. I block folks who seem obstreperous. I block large accounts who quote tweet me. And my follower count keeps rising. Slowly, but it rises. This place is better when we block generously.”

Blocking Accounts (65.3%) says Users block accounts they disagree with. Block Policy (34.7%) says Users block others liberally.

Bluesky Experience argues that Bluesky's non-algorithmic environment makes it better than Twitter. Curation of who one follows on Bluesky makes all the difference. Bluesky allows for more meaningful interactions with others. Bluesky Welcome argues that Engage with people on Bluesky. Bluesky is a great account to have. Bluesky allows for easy connection with like-minded people.

@alexjaffe.bsky.social: ““Hey Q, did you delete your BlueSky?” Helena asked. “The moment I found out they were coding it with AI,” Vic said. “But all social media has AI.” “And I’m not on any social media.” “Well, not gonna lie.”

Bluesky Experience (56.7%) says Bluesky is a better social media platform. Bluesky Welcome (43.3%) says Bluesky is a good platform to engage with people.

Sports.detail:
Game Praise argues that the game has fascinating reviews. The game is a masterpiece. The game is an all-time favorite. The game is interesting to see. Game Enjoyment argues that Games have impressive cutscenes and intense matches. Games can be engaging despite not being typical taste.

@pataloon.bsky.social: “Cool game made by a friend! It's a cave diving experience where you have to crawl into very narrow spaces (awful). A great (fucking awful) idea that they had was to shrink the screen borders when the space gets reeeaally small.”

Game Praise (60.2%) says the game is enjoyable. Game Enjoyment (39.8%) says Games are enjoyable.

Remake Review argues that the remake feels fresh to play. the remake captures the mythical vibe of the original. the remake doesn't let players figure things out for themselves. OOT Remake argues that Some enjoy playing OOT remake. Others await setup to play OOT remake.

@pudge.bsky.social: “One worrying trend I'm seeing is a consistent mistrust in the player's ability to figure shit out for themselves. Be it story beats or puzzles, the remake doesn't let you stop a second to notice details and investigate. It grabs you by the scruff and says "Over here!”

Remake Review (80%) says the remake has a different feel than the original. OOT Remake (20%) says People discuss playing OOT remake.

Culture.detail:
Russell Brand argues that Russell Brand is a rapist. Russell Brand used his image to hide his actions. Russell Brand's behavior is inexcusable. Brand Guilty argues that Brand is a psychopath who rapes people. Brand's sexual assaults were an open secret. Brand is a rapist. Brand was able to act with impunity for many years. Brand's actions need to be corrected ASAP.

@searchlightmag.bsky.social: “When Russell Brand faced allegations of sexual violence, prominent right-wing figures denounced an establishment conspiracy. Now that a jury has convicted him, their claims have been met with a conspicuous absence of public comment. Read more here:”

Russell Brand (94.3%) says Russell Brand is guilty. Brand Guilty (5.7%) says Brand is guilty of rape.

Writing Books argues that writing a novel in a short time is exhausting. writing can be inspired by teaching or reading. Writing Importance argues that writing is important.

@sugarbutch.net: “oh I actually did put a book out this year, but I kind of forgot to tell anybody the writing spicy prompt book! 398 D/s erotica prompts, one per page”

Writing Books (53.9%) says Authors share their writing experiences. Writing Importance (46.1%) says Writing is important.

Stream Updates argues that Streamers announce schedule changes. Stream Canceled argues that Streamers cancel or postpone streams.

@tuzzleton.bsky.social: “Thank you all who came to the stream! We hit our goal, and even though we didn’t hit 24 hours, we managed almost 18! I may try and make up the remainder this week. For now, I am heading back to sleep. Thank you all again so much, it means a ton to see such caring and loving folk!”

Stream Updates (63.7%) says Streamers announce schedule changes. Stream Canceled (36.3%) says Streamers cancel or postpone streams.

Environment.detail:
Bird Photos argues that sharing bird pictures is entertaining. Bird photos can be artistic with backlit lighting. Bird Appreciation argues that Birds are fascinating and beautiful.

@carlbovisnature.bsky.social: “I met this very friendly Robin at RSPB Ham Wall at the weekend. 😍 I think he wanted to be photographed, don't you? 🤔😁🐦 #birds 🪶”

Bird Photos (52.4%) says People share bird photos. Bird Appreciation (47.6%) says Birds are fascinating and beautiful.

Data Centers Harm argues that Data centers use excessive water. Data centers increase fossil fuel production. Data centers have negative climate implications. Data centers harm local communities. Gas Power argues that Gas-fired power is expensive and inefficient. Scavenged jet engines are a bad power source.

@cinematt.bsky.social: “It can’t connect data centres to the grid, it can’t build data centres, they have promised a lot of clients those data centres will exist, and used those contracts to take on an insane amount of debt. It’s not looking great.”

Data Centers Harm (77.8%) says Data centers harm the environment. Gas Power (22.2%) says Data centers use gas-fired power.

Flowers Blooming argues that flowers are blooming in my yard. native flowers are blooming on trails. a lovely bloom is chosen for a bouquet. Garden Plants argues that Some garden plants are preferred.

@justjacque.bsky.social: “Flower of the day. #Flowers #BloomScrolling #DailyFlower”

Flowers Blooming (90%) says Flowers are currently blooming. Garden Plants (10%) says Some garden plants are preferred.

COP31 Progress argues that COP31 needs to deliver real climate progress. COP31 should result in noticeable climate action. COP31 Demands argues that People demand climate action at COP31.

@guardian-climate.bsky.social: “Cop31 must deliver climate progress that people can see is real, host says: High-stakes talks involving 190 countries begin on Monday as world grapples with El Niño supercharged by fossil fuels The Cop31 summit must produce progress, “a tangible outcome ...”

COP31 Progress (83.9%) says COP31 must produce tangible climate progress. COP31 Demands (16.1%) says People demand climate action at COP31.

Other.detail:
Dream Experiences argues that dreams can be vivid and realistic. dreams can be spiritual and symbolic. Dream Significance argues that Dreams have meaning.

@remyvrc.bsky.social: “What do you think he’s dreaming about”

Dream Experiences (82.2%) says People share their dream experiences. Dream Significance (17.8%) says Dreams have meaning.

Word Choice argues that Some words are unusual or unpopular. Word Meaning argues that Words have specific meanings.

@sizu-p.bsky.social: “#megascream where words have beginnings and endings”

Word Choice (76.1%) says Some words are unusual or unpopular. Word Meaning (23.9%) says Words have specific meanings.

Wearing Unconventional argues that I wear unusual clothes to events. I wear what makes me happy despite others' opinions. Fashion Choices argues that I consider wearing a camouflage jacket. I need a new blazer for formal events. Casual wear is not suitable for business.

@drquesodelamuerte.bsky.social: “I have such a hard time being comfortable wearing dresses and Cecil Nyx just being out there smiling in a gorgeous pink dress just fucking got me 🤼‍♀️”

Wearing Unconventional (58.7%) says People wear unconventional clothes. Fashion Choices (41.3%) says People discuss their fashion choices.

Drinking Request argues that I want you to watch me drink it. He might drink excessively. Drinking Remarks argues that Posts share thoughts on drinking.

@noisyvivian.bsky.social: “The proper response to this is to lock eyes for as long as I can while drinking it, obviously.”

Drinking Request (60.6%) says Someone wants to drink something. Drinking Remarks (39.4%) says Posts share thoughts on drinking.

Hair Changes argues that I gave myself a bad haircut. I saved money by cutting my own hair. I found a product that works for my hair. Hair Styles argues that Hair styles are showcased. Hair styles are drawn. Hair styles are managed.

@retroheart.net: “Quick Cinnamon Bun doodles, I keep changing her hair style and am trying to lock down a default look”

Hair Changes (68.6%) says People discuss their hair changes. Hair Styles (31.4%) says Hair styles are discussed.
